date-released: 2026-05-24
version: "1.0"
abstract: >
  PDS (Progressive Discovery Spine) is an architectural pattern for the
  middleware layer between AI agents and enterprise backend systems. It
  addresses four documented failure modes of naive MCP deployment at scale:
  context bloat, hallucinated tool selection, missing production controls
  (retries / backpressure / observability / audit), and discovery
  anti-patterns. The pattern is defined as ten principles plus reference
  SLAs and a numbered build sequence.
